Subject: [PATCH] offer no websocket compression

With permessage-deflate, a client frame that repeats an earlier frame can
end ttyd: libwebsockets 4.3.5 fails the assertion `priv->rx.avail_out` at
extension-permessage-deflate.c:350, after it inflates the frame's trailer,
and the process aborts with SIGABRT, ending every session it serves. The
page sees a close with code 1006 and no error line.

Chrome sends such a frame for 8257 bytes whose first 8256 repeat the frame
before, so that two echo lines of one 8256 byte blob do it on the wire.
Every length seen to do it is one byte past a multiple of 258, the longest
match deflate has, such as 3097, 4129, 6193, 8257 and 12385, though not
every such length does.

Offer neither extension, so that libwebsockets never reaches that code. The
frames travel uncompressed in both directions, and nothing in the wire
protocol depends on compression.

---
 src/server.c | 11 -----------
 1 file changed, 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/server.c b/src/server.c
--- a/src/server.c
+++ b/src/server.c
@@ -30,14 +30,6 @@
                                                  {"tty", callback_tty, sizeof(struct pss_tty), 0},
                                                  {NULL, NULL, 0, 0}};
 
-#ifndef LWS_WITHOUT_EXTENSIONS
-// websocket extensions
-static const struct lws_extension extensions[] = {
-    {"permessage-deflate", lws_extension_callback_pm_deflate, "permessage-deflate"},
-    {"deflate-frame", lws_extension_callback_pm_deflate, "deflate_frame"},
-    {NULL, NULL, NULL}};
-#endif
-
 #if LWS_LIBRARY_VERSION_NUMBER >= 4000000
 static const uint32_t backoff_ms[] = {1000, 2000, 3000, 4000, 5000};
 static lws_retry_bo_t retry = {
@@ -324,9 +316,6 @@
   info.uid = -1;
   info.max_http_header_pool = 16;
   info.options = LWS_SERVER_OPTION_LIBUV | LWS_SERVER_OPTION_VALIDATE_UTF8 | LWS_SERVER_OPTION_DISABLE_IPV6;
-#ifndef LWS_WITHOUT_EXTENSIONS
-  info.extensions = extensions;
-#endif
   info.max_http_header_data = 65535;
 
   int debug_level = LLL_ERR | LLL_WARN | LLL_NOTICE;
